       1   00:0000                      ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
       2   00:0000                      ; MSX2 SCREEN 5 pinball movement demo (Z80 / SJASM)
       3   00:0000                      ;
       4   00:0000                      ; Build from the repository root:
       5   00:0000                      ;     .\sjasm.exe -s pinball.asm
       6   00:0000                      ;
       7   00:0000                      ; Output: pinball.rom (32 KiB)
       8   00:0000                      ;
       9   00:0000                      ; Controls:
      10   00:0000                      ;   cursor/joystick left  - left flipper
      11   00:0000                      ;   cursor/joystick right - right flipper
      12   00:0000                      ;   space / trigger 1     - both flippers, and launch a waiting ball
      13   00:0000                      ;
      14   00:0000                      ; The ball uses signed 8.8 fixed-point position and velocity.  The high byte of
      15   00:0000                      ; each position is the visible pixel coordinate; the low byte is the fraction.
      16   00:0000                      ; Gravity, rebounds and flipper impulses therefore remain smooth on a 3.58 MHz
      17   00:0000                      ; Z80 without multiplication or division.
      18   00:0000                      ;
      19   00:0000                      ; Reading guide
      20   00:0000                      ; -------------
      21   00:0000                      ; 1. MainLoop synchronises to VBlank, updates graphics/input, then physics.
      22   00:0000                      ; 2. StepBall applies gravity and divides movement into four collision steps.
      23   00:0000                      ; 3. ResolveTileX/Y handles the static 8x8 collision map.
      24   00:0000                      ; 4. CheckMapPolygons/Circles handles objects from Tiled's PinballObjects layer.
      25   00:0000                      ; 5. CheckFlippers handles frame-specific polygons from maps/flippers.tmx.
      26   00:0000                      ; 6. The Video section uploads generated assets and updates sprites/animations.
      27   00:0000                      ;
      28   00:0000                      ; Coordinate conventions
      29   00:0000                      ; ----------------------
      30   00:0000                      ; BALL_X/BALL_Y are the top-left of the 16x16 sprite box. Collision routines
      31   00:0000                      ; normally add 8 to obtain the ball centre. Positive X points right; positive Y
      32   00:0000                      ; points down. Consequently a negative BALL_VY means that the ball is rising.
      33   00:0000                      ;
      34   00:0000                      ; 8.8 examples: 0100h=+1.0, 0040h=+0.25, FF00h=-1.0. Stored velocities and
      35   00:0000                      ; frame movement use the same full-speed time base, which keeps collision
      36   00:0000                      ; thresholds, impulses and visible travel directly comparable.
      37   00:0000                      ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
      38   00:0000                      
      39   00:0000                              output  pinball.rom
      40   00:4000                      
