    2345   00:4DB3                      ; Copy BC bytes to an address in VRAM bank 1. Sprite tables live between
    2346   00:4DB3                      ; 07400h and 07800h; setting R#14 explicitly prevents BIOS/VDP bank state from
    2347   00:4DB3                      ; turning uninitialised SAT data into a screen full of stray sprites.
    2348   00:4DB3                      CopyToVRAMPage1:
    2349   00:4DB3                              ; R#14 selects the 16 KiB VRAM bank. The following two writes set the
    2350   00:4DB3                              ; 14-bit address with bit 6 marking a write operation.
